2026-08-16T14:54:24Z    [HAS:Net fees] GATE critic: You under-adjust for the stated disposals. Management said “the six countries that we disposed of made around GBP 15 million per annum in fees,” yet your entire post‑guidance tilt is only −1.13% on the £849.1m base (≈£9.6m), and that £9.6m is meant to cover both H2 weakness and disposals. If FY2025’s £972.4m includes those operations, FY2026 reported net fees should mechanically be reduced by about £15m for disposals alone (or pro‑rated to the actual disposal dates), before any H2 trend effects. As a result, £839.6m is too high by at least the shortfall versus the £15m disposal impact.
