2026-08-16T14:54:42Z    [HAS:Pre-exceptional basic EPS] GATE critic: You computed FY2026 pre-exceptional EPS off a pre-exceptional operating profit of £26.21m, but management’s own guidance says FY2026 pre-exceptional operating profit will be at the top of a £37–£46m range. £26.21m looks like the FY2025 actual, not FY2026. Using the guided FY2026 basis (≈£46m), EPS would be roughly (46−13.4)×(1−35.1%)/1,590.2m×100 ≈ 1.3p, not 0.52p. The proposed figure is therefore anchored to the wrong period/basis and is too low.
